    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0425" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1098a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-26T13:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5191. With regard to the “Identic Draft Declaration on German Crimes in Poland”
                    agreed on in Quebec<anchor n="17" xml:id="d425-f1"/> to be issued on August 30
                    by the British and American Governments, we believe it would be advisable to
                    give the Soviet Government for its information an advance copy of the text. We
                    propose, if the British are agreeable, to give the text to the Soviet Chargé
                    here on August 28. Please telegraph urgently if the British concur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d425-f1" n="17" xml:id="d425-f1-content">
                <p>The records of the First Quebec Conference, August 17–24, 1943, are scheduled for
                    publication in a subsequent volume of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                        Relations.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
